> [!answer]
> **1. In relation to opportunities**
> - **Scanning the environment** for changes and unmet needs; **recognising and discovering** opportunities;
> - **Generating ideas** and screening them; **evaluating** each opportunity for attractiveness, durability, timeliness and value to the buyer (feasibility analysis);
> - **Selecting and exploiting** the best opportunity within its **window of opportunity**, and continuing to innovate as the environment changes.
>
> **2. In relation to organisation**
> - **Deciding the form of business ownership** and establishing the legal entity;
> - **Designing the structure** — the tasks, roles, departments and lines of authority;
> - **Building and leading the team**: recruiting, training, motivating, delegating and rewarding;
> - **Planning, directing, co-ordinating and controlling** operations, setting the culture and vision, and building relationships with customers, suppliers and regulators.
>
> **3. In relation to resources**
> - **Identifying the resources required** — financial, human, physical, technological and informational;
> - **Mobilising/acquiring** them from the cheapest appropriate source (own savings, family, bank loan, equity investors, trade credit, leasing, government schemes);
> - **Allocating and combining** them efficiently (the entrepreneur as the co-ordinator of the factors of production), **managing cash flow**, and **bearing the risk and uncertainty** of their use;
> - **Creating value** and generating a surplus (profit) from the combination, and reinvesting it for growth.
